mmunohistochemical localization of opsin. <source>Exp. Eye Res.</source> <volume>44</volume>:<fpage>347</fpage>&#x02013;361.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2954840</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Johnson, L.V., J.C. Blanks, and G.S. Hageman. <year>1989</year>. Effects of retinal degenerations on the cone matrix sheath. <source>Prog. Clin. Biol. Res.</source> <volume>314</volume>:<fpage>217</fpage>&#x02013;232.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2608663</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Kohl, S., I. Giddings, D. Besch, E. Apfelstedt-Sylla, E. Zrenner, and B. Wissinger. <year>1998</year>. The role of the peripherin/RDS gene in retinal dystrophies. <source>Acta Anat. (Basel).</source> <volume>162</volume>:<fpage>75</fpage>&#x02013;84.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9831753</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Lebovitz, R.M., K. Takeyasu, and D.M. Fambrough. <year>1989</year>. Molecular characterization and expression of the (Na&#x0002b; &#x0002b; K&#x0002b;)-ATPase alpha-subunit in <source>Drosophila melanogaster. EMBO J.</source> <volume>8</volume>:<fpage>193</fpage>&#x02013;202.</citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Mears, A.J., M. Kondo, P.K. Swain, Y. Takada, R.A. Bush, T.L. Saunders, P.A. Sieving, and A. Swaroop. <year>2001</year>. Nrl is required for rod photoreceptor development. <source>Nat. Genet.</source> <volume>29</volume>:<fpage>447</fpage>&#x02013;452.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11694879</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Molday, R.S. <year>1998</year>. Photoreceptor membrane proteins, phototransduction, and retinal degenerative diseases. The Friedenwald Lecture. <source>Invest. Ophthalmol. Vis. Sci.</source> <volume>39</volume>:<fpage>2491</fpage>&#x02013;2513.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9856758</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Molday, R.S., D. Hicks, and L. Molday. <year>1987</year>. Peripherin. A rim-specific membrane protein of rod outer segment discs. <source>Invest. Ophthalmol. Vis. Sci.</source> <volume>28</volume>:<fpage>50</fpage>&#x02013;61.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2433249</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Musarella, M.A. <year>2001</year>. Molecular genetics of macular degeneration. <source>Doc. Ophthalmol.</source> <volume>102</volume>:<fpage>165</fpage>&#x02013;177.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11556484</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Nikonov, S.S., L.L. Daniele, X. Zhu, C.M. Craft, A. Swaroop, and E.N. Pugh Jr. <year>2005</year>. Photoreceptors of Nrl &#x02212;/&#x02212; mice coexpress functional S- and M-cone opsins having distinct inactivation mechanisms. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>125</volume>:<fpage>287</fpage>&#x02013;304.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15738050</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Nir, I., and D.S. Papermaster. <year>1986</year>. Immunocytochemical localization of opsin in the inner segment and ciliary plasma membrane of photoreceptors in retinas of rds mutant mice. <source>Invest. Ophthalmol. Vis. Sci.</source> <volume>27</volume>:<fpage>836</fpage>&#x02013;840.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2939037</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Nour, M., X.Q. Ding, H. Stricker, S.J. Fliesler, and M.I. Naash. <year>2004</year>. Modulating expression of peripherin/rds in transgenic mice: critical levels and the effect of overexpression. <source>Invest. Ophthalmol. Vis. Sci.</source> <volume>45</volume>:<fpage>2514</fpage>&#x02013;2521.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15277471</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Reuter, J.H., and S. Sanyal. <year>1984</year>. Development and degeneration of retina in rds mutant mice: the electroretinogram. <source>Neurosci. Lett.</source> <volume>48</volume>:<fpage>231</fpage>&#x02013;237.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6483282</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Ritter, L.M., K. Boesze-Battaglia, B.M. Tam, O.L. Moritz, N. Khattree, S.C. Chen, and A.F. Goldberg. <year>2004</year>. Uncoupling of photoreceptor peripherin/rds fusogenic activity from biosynthesis, subunit assembly, and targeting: a potential mechanism for pathogenic effects. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>279</volume>:<fpage>39958</fpage>&#x02013;39967.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15252042</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Sanyal, S., and H.G. Jansen. <year>1981</year>. Absence of receptor outer segments in the retina of rds mutant mice. <source>Neurosci. Lett.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>23</fpage>&#x02013;26.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7207866</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Sanyal, S., A. De Ruiter, and R.K. Hawkins. <year>1980</year>. Development and degeneration of retina in rds mutant mice: light microscopy. <source>J. Comp. Neurol.</source> <volume>194</volume>:<fpage>193</fpage>&#x02013;207.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7440795</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Steinberg, R.H., S.K. Fisher, and D.H. Anderson. <year>1980</year>. Disc morphogenesis in vertebrate photoreceptors. <source>J. Comp. Neurol.</source> <volume>190</volume>:<fpage>501</fpage>&#x02013;508.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6771304</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Stricker, H.M., X.Q. Ding, A. Quiambao, S.J. Fliesler, and M.I. Naash. <year>2005</year>. The Cys214&#x02192;Ser mutation in peripherin/rds causes a loss-of-function phenotype in transgenic mice. <source>Biochem. J.</source> <volume>388</volume>:<fpage>605</fpage>&#x02013;613.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15656787</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Tam, B.M., O.L. Moritz, and D.S. Papermaster. <year>2004</year>. The C terminus of peripherin/rds participates in rod outer segment targeting and alignment of disk incisures. <source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>15</volume>:<fpage>2027</fpage>&#x02013;2037.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14767063</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">Toda, K., R.A. Bush, P. Humphries, and P.A. Sieving. <year>1999</year>. The electroretinogram of the rhodopsin knockout mouse. <source>Vis. Neurosci.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>391</fpage>&#x02013;398.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10367972</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Travis, G.H., M.B. Brennan, P.E. Danielson, C.A. Kozak, and J.G. Sutcliffe. <year>1989</year>. Identification of a photoreceptor-specific mRNA encoded by the gene responsible for retinal degeneration slow (rds). <source>Nature.</source> <volume>338</volume>:<fpage>70</fpage>&#x02013;73.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2918924</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">van Soest, S., A. Westerveld, P.T. de Jong, E.M. Bleeker-Wagemakers, and A.A. Bergen. <year>1999</year>. Retinitis pigmentosa: defined from a molecular point of view. <source>Surv. Ophthalmol.</source> <volume>43</volume>:<fpage>321</fpage>&#x02013;334.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10025514</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal">Wrigley, J.D., C.L. Nevett, and J.B. Findlay. <year>2002</year>. Topological analysis of peripherin/rds and abnormal glycosylation of the pathogenic Pro216&#x02192;Leu mutation. <source>Biochem. J.</source> <volume>368</volume>:<fpage>649</fpage>&#x02013;655.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12207562</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="journal">Yoshida, S., A.J. Mears, J.S. Friedman, T. Carter, S. He, E. Oh, Y. Jing, R. Farjo, G. Fleury, C. Barlow, et al. <year>2004</year>. Expression profiling of the developing and mature Nrl&#x02212;/&#x02212; mouse retina: identification of retinal disease candidates and transcriptional regulatory targets of Nrl. <source>Hum. Mol. Genet.</source> <volume>13</volume>:<fpage>1487</fpage>&#x02013;1503.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15163632</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib34"><citation citation-type="journal">Yu, J., S. He, J.S. Friedman, M. Akimoto, D. Ghosh, A.J. Mears, D. Hicks, and A. Swaroop. <year>2004</year>. Altered expression of genes of the Bmp/Smad and Wnt/calcium signaling pathways in the cone-only Nrl&#x02212;/&#x02212; mouse retina, revealed by gene profiling using custom cDNA microarrays. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>279</volume>:<fpage>42211</fpage>&#x02013;42220.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15292180</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>